    "complete": true,
    "clarification_required": false,
    "rationale": "Two separate qualified records, both active semantic facts that apply repository-wide with no conditions and reviewed trust, agree that a repeated request key returns the first successful response stored in its idempotency receipt. One is under request identity, with HTTP acceptance probe evidence (fixture://quality/receipt-a). The other is under financial reconciliation, with independent queue probe evidence (fixture://quality/receipt-b). Both are kept because their evidence and provenance differ. Bounded retries passed qualification but covers transient retry behaviour, not repeats after success, so it was left out. Superseded, revoked, deadline and endpoint records and the session-recovery records cover other subjects. The transaction stream records (component:src/transactions/N) were not expanded because the component is unknown in the current context. That branch is a remaining uncertainty if the question is about a transaction stream. Both receipt records are labelled as synthetic authored assertions and have not been checked against code."
  },
